# Files in the repo that must NOT be published as public static assets.
# The asset directory is the repository root, so anything not listed here
# is downloadable from the live site.

# The git repository itself. Wrangler uploads the asset directory as-is,
# so without this the whole history is published and downloadable — and
# once the pack file passes 25 MiB the build fails outright on it.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Server-side code
worker/

# Wrangler's own build output. It bundles worker/index.js into
# .wrangler/tmp/deploy-*/index.js at deploy time, inside the asset directory,
# so without this the deploy publishes the built worker — router and all — as a
# downloadable file. Confirmed live: it returned 200 before this was added.
.wrangler/

# Full-resolution source photographs of the paintings. These are the
# originals the published .jpeg files are made from; nothing on the site
# links to them, and publishing them would hand out high-res copies of
# work the terms page explicitly forbids reproducing.
artwork/

# Build and tooling config
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml
.assetsignore
.claude/

# Local-only helpers
serve.ps1
README.md
